# Wave W17-Z (Route 215): shard post — a fallen-shard marker post at the Shardfall road’s north mouth: a weathered post carrying a fan of three small purple meteor shards at its head, marking where the crater field’s falls begin (design: fallen purple shards rising through the grass at the road’s Shardfall end — the field itself is beyond the posts, the posts stand on the road). On puddle turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 214’s meteor posts behind it by the fan entire: those carry one shard for a beginning, these carry three for a fall zone.
